    "order": "Array order within stages: sum all legacy and new relief, multiply combined delta by the original protection guard (linearity reproduces legacy exactly); carve paths in array order; restore hard protection cores; quantise; measure before committing. Always exact baseline. Existing route paths remain at baseline inside their guard. Fillets round new corners by <=12m, never alter original route geometry.",
    "widths": "Full widths. Canyon width pairs interpolate by arc length. Wall knots floor-to-rim horizontal fraction versus rise. high_side=-1 means right of directed line. Polyline corners are rounded by preprocessing in builder. Shelf high_side=+1 (left/NE); west_drop=-1 (right/east). High plateau extends to map edge, with inherited gentle relief. vertical_offset_cm chooses raised high-side Shelf versus lowered west foot, avoiding raising the entire existing world east of west_drop.",
    "masks": "2048 square uint8 raw. Row0=min world Y, col0=min world X, extrema inclusive. paths:255 corridor,1..254 shoulders. cliffs:0 other,85 talus,170 ledge/steep,255 >50 degrees. Classification from final quantised output.",
    "design_changes": [
      "Main canyon/escarpment/spire controls unchanged; corner fillets move only intervening geometry by at most 12m.",
      "scar_trail endpoint moved from (-350,-330)m to (-350,-270)m, 60m north, to meet the switchback rim instead of dropping straight to the canyon floor at an impossible trail grade.",
      "shelf_trail endpoint moved from (480,470)m to (440,435)m, 53.15m southwest, to meet the notch foot instead of ending halfway up its wall.",
      "Explicit descent traverses extend along walls around the requested anchors; two additional Scar end escapes serve isolated ends.",
      "Descent hairpins have explicit 15m-radius arc controls so the walkable corridor does not fold across a sharp polyline reversal."
    ],
    "fall_cache_risks": [
      "West_drop has no ascent: a surviving fall may leave cache inaccessible from above.",
      "Scar/Shelf ledges away from descents can strand surviving-fall caches; fatal falls retain existing last-safe-rim relocation.",
      "Canyon end caps near world boundary require traversal review."
    ],
    "run_order": [
      "Lead closes editor, builds dustfallEditor (Json is an editor-only dependency), opens foundation with sole writer lock.",
      "Run Scripts/build_phase5_terrain.py as __main__; wait for Docs/Phase5_TerrainResults.json status complete, not queue completion.",
      "Review native measurements and collision probes; run Dustfall.Core.Terrain tests and brief existing smoke.",
      "Run Scripts/capture_phase5_terrain.py as __main__; wait for Saved/Codex/Phase5Terrain/report.json and review all images.",
      "PCG rebuild is a separate task using TerrainMasks and resolved/source feature JSON."
    ],
